p=Path('docs/architecture.md');s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('Finalization, individual path queries, JSON encoding and database transactions can still block beyond that target.', 'Finalization, individual path queries and JSON encoding can still block beyond that target. Local SQLite execution is isolated as described below; its transaction still gates durable acknowledgement.')
s=s.replace('Its dense SQLite case does not meet capacity or latency targets. A long-lived worker or asynchronous writer requires committed-only read isolation and measured benefit, not a second world authority.', 'Its dense SQLite case does not meet capacity or latency targets. The measured local worker retains committed-only read isolation and one connection; further simulation/serialization isolation remains gated.')
s=s.replace('The existing long-callback suspension heuristic also remains a limitation during multi-second synchronous commits;', 'The existing long-callback suspension heuristic remains a limitation during arbitrary multi-second main-thread operations;')
s=s.replace('the adapter bounds transaction-local pending requests to 128', 'the adapter bounds transaction-local pending requests to 128')
s=s.replace('Worker exit/error fences further work without automatic replay; shutdown drains admitted work.', 'Worker exit/error fences further work without automatic replay; shutdown drains admitted work and treats exit as expected only after a close acknowledgement. External queued admissions are bounded at 256, transaction-local pending calls at 128; excess work fails explicitly. A caller cannot close the connection from inside its own transaction.')
s=s.replace('The worker\'s 128-entry statement cache stores no bound values', 'The worker\'s 128-entry statement cache stores no bound values')
